Q: NS_BINDING_ABORTED error in react useEffect() when using window.location.replace() A: <p>The reason why you’re having this issue is when redirect component mounts as part of router navigation and it <code>useEffect</code> inside the navigation commit window.</p>
<p>So for a fix with <code>useEffect</code> try:</p>
<pre><code>import { useEffect } from &quot;react&quot;;

export default function Redirect() {
  useEffect(() =&gt; {
    const id = window.setTimeout(() =&gt; {
  window.location.replace(&quot;https://google.com&quot;);
    }, 0);

    return () =&gt; window.clearTimeout(id);
  }, []);

  return null;
}
</code></pre>
<p>For a fix without <code>useEffect</code> and <code>setTimeout</code> try the <code>useLayoutEffect</code> :</p>
<pre><code>import { useLayoutEffect } from &quot;react&quot;;

export default function Redirect() {
  useLayoutEffect(() =&gt; {
    window.location.href = &quot;https://google.com&quot;;
// OR
    window.location.replace(&quot;https://google.com&quot;);
  }, []);

  return null;
}
</code></pre>

